Catch `sqlite3.Error` in the provider OAuth callback(s) (or inside `_persist_completed_provider_auth`) and convert it into a JSON `HTTPException`, consistent with other credential persistence routes, e.g.:
```python
except (OSError, SidecarError, sqlite3.Error) as error:  # <-- FIX 🟢 handle DB errors
    logger.error("Provider credential persistence failed: %s", error)
    raise HTTPException(
